{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055046-any-resources-for-historical-magic-occult-traditions","id":1055046,"title":"Any resources for historical magic/occult traditions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-25T19:49:31-08:00","id":1055046,"title":"Any resources for historical magic/occult traditions?","content":"I was wondering if anyone knew any books or websites for magic/occult traditions, for thematic purposes.<br /> <br /> Today I was browsing Chapters bookstore and came across The Occult, Witchcraft and Magic: An Illustrated History by Christopher Dell.<br /> <br /> I flipped through it and apparently it attempts to incorporates culturally appropriate art to different magical traditions. It also briefly introduces the reader to belief systems and practices surrounding a particular magic (be it Pagan, Wiccan, Mesopotamian, Voodoo, Latinoamerican Catholic/Voodoo, etc.) I thought this might be a more in-depth alternative to the Mage: Magical Traditions book, but I could not be certain.<br /> <br /> My goal is to saturate myself in magical traditions for the purposes of creating a more aware narrative. I've never been interested in magic or occult stuff before, so it feels kind of weird to push forward when I have such limited knowledge.<br /> <br /> Any help would be awesome, homies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:24:42-08:00","id":1055073,"title":"","content":"1E book <b>Magical Traditions</b> is good resources on number of Sleepers occult Traditions and how they would be used in <b>Mage</b>. With 2E rules you will need to convert them to <i>Mystery Cult Intiation</i> Merit for Nameless Order they would be in 2E setting, but it's fun to read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:30:10-08:00","id":1055075,"title":"","content":"Well, while it's not exactly superbly in-depth, <a href=\"http://www.mythologydictionary.com/\" target=\"_blank\">the Mythology Dictionary</a> is a good surface view.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}